      "content": "look, i'm not trying to be offensive, i'm literally just a student trying to write a paper. if i can't even look up the actual arguments used in history to understand how political systems work, how am i supposed to learn? \n\nit's pretty important for my essay to understand how they used things like \"social order\" or \"cultural preservation\" as justifications. can you at least explain what kind of academic or sociological theories were being cited by people at that time to defend those policies? i just need the historical context for my research.",
